\cf0 Pricing Decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 Base price is set at $39.99 per subject, one-time purchase. This is above the original $29.99 hypothesis and reflects three considerations:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Quality signal: $29.99 reads as a mobile app. $39.99 reads as a product someone built carefully. In an edtech purchase made by a parent on behalf of a student taking a high-stakes exam, the higher price likely improves conversion rather than hurting it.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Margin against variable costs: AI inference costs, payment processing, and refunds are all variable. The $10 difference gives meaningful buffer against any of these running higher than modeled.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Referral program headroom: A 20% referral fee at $29.99 is $6 \'97 not meaningful enough to motivate a tutor recommendation. At $39.99 it is $8, which is a credible incentive for a recurring referral relationship.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 A tiered pricing structure (base access vs. unlimited) remains a future option to be evaluated once August usage data establishes what a typical session costs. No context cap will be implemented for the launch.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

