\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The Subscription Problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 Approximately 85% of students who take an AP exam take 5 or fewer over their entire high school career. Subscription products price for a student who takes 10 subjects across 4 years \'97 a profile that represents a small minority of the addressable market.\
The practical consequence: a student taking 3 subjects spread across two school years pays for two full years of Albert or Fiveable access and may use each subscription intensively for only 3\'964 weeks. The one-time purchase model is not just more affordable \'97 it is structurally more honest about how AP prep is actually consumed.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Variable Cost Model\
AI Inference\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 AI inference is the primary variable cost and the one with the most uncertainty at this stage. The key inputs are:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Sessions per user: placeholder 6 (light user = 3, heavy user = 10). August data will replace this.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Exchanges per session: estimated 10, mixing MC, instruction, and FRQ turns.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Input tokens per exchange: ~2,500, including the session-opening system prompt that loads canonical content, student activity record, and scoring criteria. This system prompt is likely the single largest input cost driver per session.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Output tokens per exchange: ~500. FRQ criterion feedback runs ~600 tokens; MC responses ~150. Mix matters significantly.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Model rates: Claude Sonnet ~$3.00/1M input, ~$15.00/1M output. Update when model selection is finalized.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 At base assumptions, inference cost per user runs approximately $1.35\'96$3.50 depending on session intensity. The inference sensitivity table in the financial model shows cost per user across a range of session counts and output token rates.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Other Variable Costs\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\fs22 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Payment processing: Stripe standard 2.9% + $0.30 per transaction. At $39.99, approximately $1.46 per sale.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Referral fees: 20% of sale price = $8.00 per referred user. Performance-based; no budget cap. Cost scales directly with referral channel success.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Support: $1.00 per user placeholder. Adjust as support volume becomes visible.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Refunds: 5% rate assumed. Higher in early periods if grading quality is questioned.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Contribution Margin at Base Assumptions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 At $39.99 price, 6 sessions, and base inference assumptions, estimated contribution per user is approximately $30\'9634 after all variable costs. Contribution margin in the 75\'9685% range. This is directional until August usage data is available.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Acquisition Cost Framework\
Fixed Spend Channels\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 Two fixed channels where budget is set monthly and results are optimized over time:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Influencer / creator spend: Monthly budget input in model. Starting hypothesis $500/month for Spring 2027 push.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Paid social / ads: Monthly budget input in model. Starting hypothesis $500/month. Platform mix TBD (Instagram, TikTok).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf3 Conversion rate assumption: 2\'963% on paid social (industry benchmark for edtech). August campaigns will replace this with actuals. Current CPC placeholder is $1.50 \'97 replace after first campaign.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Performance Channels\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 Referral is structured as a performance channel \'97 no budget, cost triggered only by successful sales. Design intent: tutors recommend Cramapple as a between-session drilling tool. Cramapple does the repetitive FRQ practice that tutors do not want to spend session time on.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Referral fee: 20% of sale ($8.00 at $39.99)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}No budget cap \'97 scales with program success\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Referral % of users estimated at 0% at launch, growing to 10\'9615% by Spring 2027 as tutor channel matures\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Formal referral program infrastructure not required for August launch\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 CAC Dynamics\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 Two CAC views are tracked in the financial model:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Paid-channel CAC: Total paid spend divided by paid-channel users only. This is the true cost of buying a customer through advertising.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Blended CAC: Total paid spend divided by all users, including organic and referral. Organic and referral users dilute CAC significantly. As word of mouth and the tutor referral channel mature, blended CAC will fall even with flat ad spend.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf3 For a one-time purchase product with no LTV beyond the initial transaction, CAC payback is immediate. The question is whether CAC is below contribution margin per user. At base assumptions it is \'97 substantially. The risk is if conversion rates are lower than modeled or inference costs run higher than expected.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Key Metrics\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs22 \cf3 Revenue per user and CAC are the primary metrics. Supporting metrics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa80\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Inference cost per user: tracked by session intensity. Replaces placeholder after August.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Contribution margin per user: net revenue minus all variable costs per user. Target $30+.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Blended CAC: target below $15 once referral and organic channels are contributing.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Refund rate: flag if it exceeds 8% \'97 signals grading quality issue.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}Referral conversion: percentage of users acquired through referral channel. Leading indicator of tutor channel health.\
